      "current_title": "Show HN: Trading cards made with e-ink displays",
      "excerpt": "I made a thing! In 2014, I was holding a stack of iPhones and thought to myself: \"Hey, if I had each phone display a playing card, I could click a button and they'd shuffle themselves\" I pared that idea all the way down to this: trading cards made of e-ink displays. Right now, each card costs me about $20 each, but with only a bit more scale, I think I can get that down to $10. In doing this project, I learned how to design electronics and circuit boards. I learned Rust and w",
